  "meaning": "A wordform proofing gauge holds four replaceable engraved type blocks beneath a stepped dictionary-profile bridge. A copper sliding stop, a spare upright affix insert, keyed block seats, hex fasteners, a knurled adjuster, and engraved scales describe wordform and affix comparison. Large uppercase Blender letterforms are recessed into substantial steel blocks and filled with textured rust-brown oxide inlays. Detailed machined construction, actual recessed marks, separate fasteners, brushed polished steel, dark red-brown granular corrosion islands with broken oxide rims, pitted normal relief and dull oxidized metal between crusts, graphite interiors, directional softbox reflections, and genuine transparent negative space.",
